125. Valid Palindrome

Description:
Given a string s, check whether it is a palindrome after:

Converting uppercase letters to lowercase.
Removing all non-alphanumeric characters (spaces, commas, symbols, etc.).

Return true if it is a palindrome, otherwise return false.

Test Case:

Input:  s = "A man, a plan, a canal: Panama"
Output: true

Why?
After removing spaces and symbols and converting to lowercase:

"amanaplanacanalpanama"

It reads the same forward and backward, so the answer is true.

class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(String s) {

        StringBuilder string = new StringBuilder();

        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            char ch = s.charAt(i);

            if (Character.isLetterOrDigit(ch)) {
                string.append(Character.toLowerCase(ch));
            }
        }

        String original = string.toString();
        String reversed = string.reverse().toString();

        return original.equals(reversed);
    }
}
